endencies and critical path. Develop and deliver progress reports, proposals, requirements documentation, and presentations. Build, develop, and maintain relationships vital to the success of the project. REPORTS TO Director, Curriculum Development and Delivery QUALIFICATIONS EDUCATION: Bachelor’s Degree in a discipline related to higher education, communication, or project management Professional certificate in a discipline related to communications or project management EXPERIENCE: Seven years of experience in the online, higher education environment, including: Two years of management or supervisory experience in higher education work related to online course development Experience at working both independently and in a team-oriented, collaborative environment is essential SKILLS, KNOWLEDGE OR ABILITIES RELATED TO THE JOB Ability to adapt to shifting priorities, demands and timelines through analytical and problem-solving capabilities and to execute tasks to meet variable deadlines Strong analytical skills including the ability to quickly identify potential issues and risk and craft innovative solutions Ability to make project adjustments and alterations promptly and efficiently Excellent communication skills including the ability to translate broad concepts into functional scope and specifications Ability to elicit cooperation from a wide variety of sources, including upper management, clients, and other departments Strong working knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite Strong written and oral communication skills Strong interpersonal skills Customer service skills an asset WORKING CONDITIONS Office based The salary for the above position is determined by the Collective Agreement with the Canadian Union of Public Employees, Local 4879, as it presently exists. Pay Band $36.62 - $40.69 ( CUPE Grade 10 (90% - 100%) ) Salary rate Please Note: This position may be subject to a 90% salary for the first 560 hours of employment. Location Kamloops, BC CA (Primary) # of Hires